DISABILITY INSURANCE POLICY

This Disability Insurance Policy (the "Policy") is entered into by and between SureGuard Insurance Company, a legal entity duly incorporated and existing under the laws of the State of Delaware, with its principal place of business at 3520 Market Street, Philadelphia, PA 19104 (hereinafter "SureGuard"), and the Insured, Nancy J. Estrada, residing at 13565 Gina Forge, Apt. 661, Dallas, TX 75243.

I. INSURANCE COVERAGE

SureGuard agrees to provide disability insurance coverage to the Insured, subject to the terms, conditions, and limitations set forth herein.

II. DEFINITION OF DISABILITY

"Disability" means that, as a result of injury or illness, the Insured is unable to perform the material and substantial duties of their regular occupation for a period exceeding 180 consecutive days.

III. BENEFIT PERIOD

The Benefit Period for this Policy is two years, commencing on the date that Disability is first established in accordance with the terms of this Policy.

IV. PREMIUMS

The premium for this Policy is $200 per month, payable on the first day of each calendar month. The first premium payment is due on the date this Policy is issued.

V. EXCLUSIONS

This Policy does not cover any disability resulting from:

a. Self-inflicted injuries or suicide or any attempt thereat;
b. War or act of war, whether declared or not;
c. Participation in a riot or insurrection;
d. Commission of a felony or any other illegal act;
e. Use of any drug, narcotic, or other controlled substance, unless prescribed by a physician;
f. Service in the armed forces or auxiliary units of any country or international authority, except as required by law.

